       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 400 mg once daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum for sertraline in adults, which is 200 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, GI effects, and agitation. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nCould you check which of these applies?\n\n1. **The dose was a typo.** Usual dosing is 50 mg daily to start, and it can be titrated up to 200 mg daily. I can enter 50, 100, or 200 mg once daily, or whatever dose you intend.\n2. **The dose is intentional.** Maybe a psychiatry consult recommended it for a specific reason. If so, please confirm the dose and the rationale. I can enter it with a note saying it exceeds the usual maximum and was clinician-verified. Pharmacy will probably want to review it.\n\nTell me which one and I'll enter the order."
